        "id": 62660,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-12T03:01:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"DrScott\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> DrScott:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As to the OP, I usually solve your problem by asking noobs who their favorite comic character is, and then working from there. &nbsp;Usually I will get at least one Superman or Batman, which I think is great as Legacy and Wraith are such good team players.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah, the problem there is me. I'm not a comic fan*, and know pretty much nothing beyond the basic basics (i.e. what Batman and Spider-Man and Superman can do). So if I asked that question I'd end up hearing the names of characters I've never even heard of and wouldn't be able to recommend a Sentinels hero anyway! Yeah, I suck. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You're understandably wondering what I'm doing here if I don't like comics. Well, I usually buy the games for my RPG club and it was pointed out that we didn't have a superhero-themed game. I researched, and chose SotM thinking that the guys would like it but it wouldn't be for me. Of course I found out that it's actually awesome and that you don't have to be into the whole superhero thing to love it.</li>\n</ul>",
